  "sourceTransforms": [
    {
      "before": "        var plan = new LanczosPlan(source, context); long temporary = 0;",
      "after": "        if (source == target) return CreateIdentity(source, context);\n        var plan = new LanczosPlan(source, context); long temporary = 0;"
    },
    {
      "before": "    internal static (long First, long Last) Support(",
      "after": "    // An unchanged axis has exact integer sample locations: sinc is one at\n    // the center and zero at every other integer in the radius-three support.\n    // Store only that contribution, so retained rows track actual live users.\n    private static LanczosPlan CreateIdentity(int length, OperationContext context)\n    {\n        var plan = new LanczosPlan(length, context);\n        try\n        {\n            var windowsBytes = 32 + length * 16L;\n            Buffer(windowsBytes); context.Reserve(windowsBytes); plan.storage += windowsBytes;\n            context.Cancellation.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();\n            plan.Windows = new Window[length];\n            var weightsBytes = 32 + length * 4L;\n            Buffer(weightsBytes); context.Reserve(weightsBytes); plan.storage += weightsBytes;\n            context.Cancellation.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();\n            plan.Weights = new int[length]; plan.MaximumCount = 1;\n            for (var x = 0; x < length; x++)\n            {\n                context.Cancellation.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();\n                plan.Windows[x] = new(x, 1, x); plan.Weights[x] = (int)One;\n            }\n            return plan;\n        }\n        catch { plan.Dispose(); throw; }\n    }\n\n    internal static (long First, long Last) Support("
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "One unchanged Lanczos axis currently retains up to7tap slots per output though exactly one weight is nonzero. Generate its canonical1tap Q30 identity directly. This removes coefficient preparation,zero-weight traversal and unnecessary ring-cache rows in required one-axis resizing. It is architectural preparation/storage work,not tuning an assumed CPUgap in the eight passing two-axis controls.",
  "intendedEndState": "CreateIdentity owns the same LanczosPlan/windows/weights under the caller OperationContext before allocation. OneWindow(x,1,x) and exactQ30One per sample,MaximumCount1. No raw coefficient scratch,trigonometry or secondary normalization. The existing exact/FMA kernels,repair,workspace ownership and public plan remain shared;smaller tap counts naturally size their storage. NonidentityCreatebody/Support/Kernel and all other production bodies remain verbatim. No new API,cache,pool or governor.",
  "proof": "When source==target=n,Support center is exactlyx. The integer numerator before double division is2*n*(sample-x);within radius3 its exact value and denominator2*n are representable and quotient is the exact integer offset. Kernel gives1at0 and0at\u00b11,\u00b12,\u00b13;edge clamping adds only zero duplicates. Original normalized/cumulativeQ30 weights are therefore exactlyOneatx and0elsewhere. New windows retain the identical effective coefficients. Exact integer/rational samples are unchanged. FMA certificates use actualsmaller term counts;zero-weight taps were already skipped before accumulation. Required rows now follow actualusers;existing controls must prove all final managed samples exact. Nonidentitybody reconstructs by reversing only the guard/helper addition.",
